# Build and packaging output
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# Node, from the wasm32 CI check
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# Credentials. wrangler writes an OAuth token under here after
# `wrangler login`; it is a deploy credential for the whole Workers
# account and must never reach a commit.
.wrangler/
.dev.vars
.env
.env.*
*.pem

# Generated worksheets. These are OUTPUT — one per audit, containing a
# specific dashboard's metric names. `ws.csv` was committed by accident
# on the first real commit. `examples/` holds the inputs; the outputs
# belong to whoever ran it.
ws.csv
*_blast_radius.csv
*-worksheet.csv
redd-*.md

# The local history store. Contains the operator's metric names — the
# first thing this tool writes to disk persistently — and is theirs, not
# ours. Ignored by default; HISTORY_STORE_PREREG.md says so on the page
# where the design is argued.
.redd/

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# NOT IGNORED, on purpose:
#
#   demo/            build output, but it is what gets deployed, and
#                    CI checks it against source rather than rebuilding
#                    blind. Ignoring it would hide drift.
#   *.csv            the corpora ARE the evidence. Every pre-registered
#                    result in REAL_DASHBOARDS.md is checkable only if
#                    the data it was scored against is here. ~2 MB.
#   *_report.html    generated, but they are the published artefacts
#                    those documents refer to.
